course: dictionary
lesson: 4160
title: Words from the sundial
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gnomon is the stick on a sundial that casts a shadow, and the shadow shows the time. You can work out the meaning from the words around it. «A sundial tells the time by the shadow of a stick called a gnomon, which moves round as the Earth turns.» The words "a stick" tell you it is a thing, and "the shadow" tells you its job.
explain: The second sentence says the same idea in other words: «A sundial is a stick, called a gnomon, that throws a shadow onto marks.» When two sentences agree, you can be more sure of the meaning. Try it: "the stick that throws the shadow" fits in both sentences, so your meaning is right.
explain: Gnomon has a second meaning in maths. It is the L-shaped piece left when a smaller, similar shape is cut out of the corner of a bigger one, such as a square. The spelling stays the same, so the context tells you which meaning is used: a sundial, or a shape.
fact: A gnomon is the part of a sundial that sticks up and casts the shadow.
fact: The shadow of the gnomon shows the time as the Earth turns.
fact: In maths, a gnomon is the L-shaped piece left when a smaller similar shape is cut from the corner of a larger one.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the context to see which one is used.
fact: The plural of gnomon is gnomons.
exercise: «A sundial tells the time by the shadow of a stick called a gnomon.» What does gnomon mean? | The sun itself | The numbers painted on a clock face | *The part of a sundial that sticks up and casts a shadow | A small hole in the ground
exercise: Mia says a gnomon is a kind of cake. Which words in «A sundial is a stick, called a gnomon, that throws a shadow» prove her wrong? | The word "is" | Nothing, she is right | Only the word "sundial" | *The words "a stick" and "a shadow"
exercise: In maths, what is a gnomon? | *The L-shaped piece left when a smaller similar shape is cut from a larger shape's corner | A type of circle | A triangle with three equal sides | The line that measures the edge of a square
test: «The gnomon threw a long shadow across the marks at noon.» In this sentence, the shadow shows what? | *The time of day | The weather | The colour of the marks | How old the sundial is
test: Which meaning of gnomon fits the sentence «The gnomon left over was the L-shaped piece cut from the corner of the square»? | Sundial: the stick that casts a shadow | Garden: a small statue | Clock: the hour hand | *Maths: the L-shaped piece
exam: Jayden says gnomon must mean a clock because the sentence talks about time. What is the best answer? | Yes, a gnomon is a clock | Context is never useful, so ignore it | The word is too hard, so skip it and forget it | *The context shows a gnomon is the stick that casts the shadow, and a clock is a different thing
